{"input": "Summarize the discussion about trend watching and appearance design.", "answers": ["The marketing put forward three noteworthy aspects in trends. First and foremost, people loved fancy things that they could be identified with. The second point was that as a remote control it had to be technologically innovative. Thirdly, being easy to use was also necessary. From a broader perspective, fruit and vegetables were in fashion this year and being spongy was also popular. Thus, contrary to the industrial designer, the marketing thought rubber was more feasible in terms of sponginess. The group agreed that the product should resemble fruit and vegetable in shape and colour but the specific design was not decided."], "length": 6957, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about trend watching and appearance design focused on the importance of having a fancy and technologically innovative remote control. The project manager emphasized the need for the remote control to have a nice look and feel, be technologically innovative, and be easy to use. The marketing expert discussed the current trends in big cities like Paris and Milan, suggesting that this year things should have a fruit and vegetable way of look or feel. The project manager agreed and mentioned that the trends are similar in many areas. The marketing expert also mentioned that the remote control should be spongy and have a fruit-like shape, but the project manager suggested that titanium might not be a good idea. The marketing expert agreed and suggested using rubber instead. The project manager asked if the remote control could be made to smell like fruit, and the marketing expert agreed. The project manager then asked about the location and features of the remote control, and the marketing expert suggested that the fancy features would be a good selling point. The project manager agreed and suggested exploring the options of making the remote control smell like fruit or be spongy. The user interface designer suggested making a fruit-shaped titanium remote control, but the project manager pointed out that they cannot do double-curved shapes. The user interface designer agreed and suggested making a banana-shaped remote control. The project manager agreed and asked the user interface designer to explore both options."}
