{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["This was a Children, Young People and Education Committee, and it was the scrutiny session with a focus on higher and further education. This whole meeting was conducted in a question and answer format. They firstly started with a question related to the trend of secondary school teachers recruiting situations, and the reasons for this, and the steps they had taken to mitigate this trend. Then they had a discussion on the decision made by the education workforce council not to accredit the University of South Wales with the ability to deliver teacher training. After this, there were some questions and answers related to the reform and reconfiguration of the post-16 education sector, equality of opportunity and university mergers. In addition, the parity of esteem between academic and vocational post-16 education and funding allocation were also discussed. Then they talked about the regional skills partnerships and the pay dispute situation. At last, they shared some opinions on 'legalised cheating'."], "length": 13866, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discusses various topics related to education in Wales. The Cabinet Secretary for Education, Kirsty Williams, and other officials are present to answer questions from the committee members. The discussion covers issues such as teacher recruitment, Welsh language provision in education, and the impact of the Diamond reforms on part-time study. The committee also inquires about the Welsh Government's plans for the post-compulsory education and training reforms, the parity of esteem between academic and vocational education, and the support for students' mental health."}
