{"input": "Summarize their discussion on the decision of not accrediting the University of South Wales with the ability to deliver teacher training.", "answers": ["Kirsty Williams firstly made it clear that it would not be appropriate to comment this since this process was independent of Government. Hefin David then proposed the impact on students and staff. Kirsty Williams thought there would be a responsibility upon the University of South Wales to ensure that those students already in the system were able to complete their studies with the appropriate level of support and tuition to enable them to achieve their career aspirations and graduate from that program. The same was true for staff. Kirsty Williams thought that would be a matter for the institution. After this, they had some discussions on the geographic spread of provision."], "length": 13883, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Cabinet Secretary for Education, Kirsty Williams, stated that the decision is independent of the Government and she has confidence in the Education Workforce Council (EWC) that made the decision. She also mentioned that there is an appeal process ongoing and the decision may potentially change the nature of the people from whom places are commissioned."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["Firstly, User Interface suggested trendy and one-color cases, good icons on the big buttons since they would be recognizable and excite the young people. Secondly, Industrial Designer introduced that young people favored soft materials and primary colors, but trendy design on the button and the use of LCD display would increase cost since the budget had always been a big problem. Moreover, the team would aim at the younger market based on the decision of the former meeting and agreed that to make the device more profitable they should sell the product for longer than one year. The team also discussed the button function of the remote control but they had not come to an agreement. Lastly, Project Manager decided on a normal battery and no kinetic to control the budget."], "length": 6026, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the design of a remote control for a television. The participants discussed various aspects such as the shape, buttons, and materials to be used. They also discussed the costs associated with different components like the display and the battery. The meeting concluded with the decision to create two different concepts for the remote control, one with a display and one without."}
