{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The meeting began with a discussion on the TORRENT project completion being pushed for two years. Grad F then introduced intermediate categorization, which was his topic for his qualification exams. The team then discussed mean subtraction from SRI. Using it had led to an improvement in Meeting Recorder digits though near mic performance worsened. The professor points to pre-echoes as the culprit. The team continued to study differences between SRI and Aurora. The team thought it would be interesting to do the Aurora tests with the SRI system instead of the HTK. The team was also exploring the Wiener filter and VTS. The professor did not seem too excited about the VTS."], "length": 11881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discusses the progress of various projects and research. The participants discuss their work on speech recognition, including the use of TIMIT and Switchboard datasets. They also discuss the implementation of a high-pass filter and the potential benefits of removing low-energy sections from speech. Additionally, they discuss the use of mean subtraction and its impact on speech recognition performance. The meeting concludes with a discussion of the reverberation time in the meeting room and the potential effects of mean subtraction on the signal-to-noise ratio."}
