{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The meeting was mainly about the exchange of the preliminary ideas about a new TV remote control project. They first got used to the writeboard and drew some animals with it.Project manager wanted to sell this remote control for twenty five Euro and expected profit will be around fifty million Euro. Afterwards the team raised different opinions about features of the new remote controls and related questions about market potential. Among all the features, having a good look and size were unanimously considered to be the most essential."], "length": 6381, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting started with the Project Manager introducing himself and explaining the agenda for the kick-off meeting. The team discussed the project plan, tools, and the design process. They also drew an animal on the Smartboard to practice using the tools. The team discussed their current remote controls and ideas for a universal remote control. They decided to keep the design original and trendy, with a focus on usability and international recognition. The team also discussed the materials and technologies to be used in the design."}
{"input": "What did Kirsty Williams say about the trend of teacher recruiting, the reasons for it, and the steps they had taken?", "answers": ["Even though there was no specific figure that could be provided, they had only been recruiting about 65 percent of targets.Therefore, there was a lot of work they have to do about this. First, they were making sure that their ITE provision was world class, and recently they were through an accreditation process for a new ITE provision that would start in the next academic year. Second, they had looked at financial incentives.Third, they were embarking on their first national ITE recruitment marketing exercise. Kirsty Williams mentioned that this was not a unique issue in Wales, but a common issue across the globe. Money was not the only reason that prevented people from getting onto these courses. What's more, from next year, they would be going to have their unique part-time PGCE route into qualification, which allowed people to bring their outside world experience into teaching, and this could increase the diversity in their teaching workforce."], "length": 13883, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Kirsty Williams said that there was still a job of work to understand and respond to the needs of teacher recruitment. She mentioned that they had made their ITE provision world-class, looked at financial incentives, and were embarking on an IT recruitment marketing exercise."}
{"input": "What did the team discuss about the use of advanced chips and LCD display?", "answers": ["Industrial Designer introduced both simple chips and advanced chips could be used for the mouse. But it would require the use of LCD display, which would highly increase the cost. Project Manager agreed that the LCD was easy when using the scroll buttons and could see the number. But Project Manager argued that young people were less likely to have their own room to afford a LCD TV and decided not to choose the advanced ones."], "length": 6036, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed the use of advanced chips and LCD display, with the Industrial Designer mentioning that it would increase costs and the Project Manager suggesting that it might not be within their budget."}
